  "reason": "The evidence strongly identifies config_029 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) as the best at 0.725 accuracy. The 2×2 grid for this encoder pair (transformer/avgpool × weighted/concat) is missing only the avgpool+concat corner (config_005). Testing it completes the grid and definitively confirms that transformer+weighted is optimal within the best encoder combination, ruling out any residual uncertainty. While config_005 is almost certainly worse (avgpool underperformed transformer by ~0.02 and concat underperformed weighted by ~0.004 in analogous settings), it is the most informative remaining experiment in the high-performing region. No other untested configuration (scgpt or pca_n2000 encoders, singleprofile, or resnet50) has a plausible path to exceed 0.725 given the large performance gaps observed. Expected cost is moderate (~4.5 GPU hours, comparable to config_042 at 4.82 with avgpool and vit_l), bringing the total to ~38 GPU hours."
}

